# Theme Editor sidebar crop lies (HARD)

**Owner 2026-08-31.** Agents kept “fixing” Home split-hero from the Theme Editor preview (sidebar open). That preview is **narrower** than full desktop. `object-fit: cover` in a **width-fluid** media column therefore shows **full figure in TE** and **legs-only / cut feet at full width**. Andrew cannot keep re-litigating this.

## Why it happens (do not re-discover)

| Viewport | Media column | Cover result on portrait photo |
|---|---|---|
| TE + left sidebar | ~narrow | Closer to portrait → more of figure visible (“fits”) |
| Full browser / sidebar closed | Wide (e.g. 62% of 1440) | Landscape-ish box → cover zooms → head/torso gone or feet wrong |

**TE crop ≠ storefront crop.** Never claim done from TE alone.

## HARD — before any “hero crop fixed” claim

1. Verify at **full desktop width ≥ 1280** (preferably **1440**) with TE sidebar **closed** or via storefront preview URL — not the narrow editor pane.
2. Also check one **TE-narrow** width (~900) — crop must **match** full width (same figure: head + feet).
3. If crops differ → the CSS is still width-fluid cover. **Stop.** Use portrait-locked frame (see `split-hero.css`) or ask — do not thrash `contain` / pad / focal for another hour.
4. Screenshot or CDP measure both widths before sending Andrew a link.

## Forbidden

- Approving / linking a hero crop after only looking at Theme Editor with sidebar open
- “Fixed” by changing only `object-position` while the media box is still full-column fluid cover
- Reintroducing cream/white gaps beside the photo (fill color must **match photo studio bg**)
- Circling TE-fit ↔ full-width-broken without the dual-width check

## Correct pattern (Home split-hero)

- Column stays layout % (e.g. 62/38)
- **`object-fit: contain`** so head + feet stay visible at TE width and full desktop
- Column `background` = studio fill matching the photo (TE: Studio fill) — pink continuing, not cream
- Never width-fluid `cover` for this portrait hero
- Skill: `barreletics-te-vs-fullwidth-crop`

